# Cyrius — Language Reference (Index)
# How to read, write, and reason about Cyrius programs.
# Replaces the monolithic content/cyrius/language.cyml (4144 lines, 73 entries)
# split during vidya v2.4.3 into 6 surface-area files.
#
# Compiler-internal patches, bug-pin retrospectives, and release-arc
# narrative were moved to content/cyrius/field_notes/compiler/ for later
# review and cleanup. Resolved patches were dropped — the fix is in the
# compiler now and no agent action is needed.
#
# Verified on Cyrius 6.5.10 (current as of 2026-08-07 — an OPEN minor;
# v6.5.0 opened it with public/private visibility, v6.4.82 was the
# prior v6.4.x closeout). The v6.0.0
# cycle opened 2026-05-19 with the two-binary rename ceremony: cyrc → cybs
# (Cyrius Bootstrap) + cc5 → cycc (Cyrius Computer Compiler).
# Bootstrap chain is now seed (asm) → cybs → cycc. v5.x closed
# at v5.11.69 after 70 slots over 11 days — longest minor in
# Cyrius history. v6.0.x closed at v6.0.91 (91 patches: rename
# ceremony + native TLS 1.2/1.3 + the CYRIUS_TARGET_AGNOS userspace
# target + the macOS/Windows cross-OS reckoning — see
# retros/v60x.cyml). mabda 3.0 fold was DROPPED from v5.11.x at
# .67-.68 boundary; folded into stdlib at 3.0.1 in v6.0.x. cycc
# self-host byte-identical at 1,141,792 B (v6.5.10; check.sh 162 / 0
# failed; self_compile 648 / 652 ms; 260 .tcyr; api-surface 4817 public
# fns; heap map 100 regions / 0 overlaps — see the region-count note
# under the v6.4.x closeout block below, the number reached 100
# again by a DIFFERENT route than the pre-.75 100; seed 29,024 B →
# cybs → cycc byte-identical; 41 shell gates under tests/*.sh, ALL
# live — 31 registered by exact path in programs/checks/main.cyr, the
# other 10 via named gate fns such as _heapmap_gate; docs that say
# "10" or "19" here are wrong and were being incremented rather than
# re-derived).
# ⚠ SELF_COMPILE IS NOISIER THAN THE DELTA: v6.5.8 measured
# 649 / 670 / 701 ms from the SAME binary. Quote the series, never
# one figure — and a byte-identical binary CANNOT have regressed, so
# check the sha before triaging a perf number.
# Size history: 1,141,784 B at v6.5.9; 1,141,696 B at v6.5.8;
# 1,133,440 B at v6.5.6; 1,124,968 B at v6.5.0; 1,108,368 B at
# v6.4.82; 1,103,512 B at v6.4.72;
# byte-identical v6.4.31→v6.4.32, .32 being cx-backend-only; the
# v6.4.10→v6.4.32 span added the aarch64 NEON / Win64 PE value-form /
# cx SIMD backends (Phase 5 complete on all four); the SIMD x86 arc +
# the v6.4.10 top-level-array-sizing fix grew
# cycc from the v6.4.0 / v6.3.45 floor of 1,024,552 B; was
# 1,071,936 B at v6.2.33, 1,069,688 B
# at v6.2.22, 1,055,784 B at v6.2.0, 1,050,608 B at v6.1.41, 874,240 B at the
# v6.0.0 cut — the v6.2.0 +5,176 B was the Phase-0 growable-table
# infra (fixup_tbl/fn-tables/codebuf grow fns + per-driver inits);
# the v6.1.x growth was the TS frontend + JS emitter + the 64 KB TS
# parse scratch + the Windows-pillar work; the v6.2→v6.3 SHRINK
# to 1,024,552 B is DCE-floor + heap-map consolidation across the
# minor. Stdlib module count: 99
# lib/*.cyr (after the bayan + ganita data/math carve, v6.1.25/.26;
# lib/sys.cyr system-introspection added v6.1.28; lib/async.cyr
# cooperative-Future runtime v6.3.11; lib/chrono.cyr DateTime/Duration
# v6.4.67; protobuf/freelist etc.).
# cycc_aarch64 685,312 B / cycc_win 1,021,440 B / cycc_cx 606,104 B
# cross-builds (v6.5.10 gate run).
# Cross-OS: ecb (macOS-arm64) · ach (Intel-Mac x86-macho) · cass
# (Windows PE) · pi (aarch64) all SELFHOST_OK + VR-01 LIBTEST_OK on
# REAL hardware at v6.5.10.
# Open queue: 16 issues · 2 proposals · 295 archived.
#
# Vendored stdlib pins at v6.5.10 (each RE-DERIVED from the `# Version:`
# header in lib/<name>.cyr — sakshi uses `# Bundled distribution of
# sakshi vX` instead, which is how sweep after sweep has skipped it;
# 7 of the 11 had drifted since the v6.4.82 stamp):
# sandhi 1.9.9 · sankoch 2.7.6 · sigil 3.12.2 · patra 1.12.12 ·
# yukti 2.3.2 · mabda 4.0.8 · bayan 1.4.1 · ganita 1.0.4 ·
# niyama 1.0.6 · vani 1.1.3 · sakshi 2.4.8.
#
# ─── v6.5.x IN FLIGHT (v6.5.10, 2026-08-07) ───
# An OPEN minor. What a USER of the language gets that they did not
# have at v6.4.86:
# - **`private` / `public` visibility** (.0) — the language's first
#   enforced encapsulation boundary. File-scoped opt-in: a file with no
#   `private` declaration behaves exactly as before, which is why the
#   ecosystem's blast radius on adoption day was zero. Private items
#   also drop out of the exported symbol table and `cyrius api-surface`.
#   See features.cyml `visibility_public_private_v650`.
# - **Threaded programs can EXIT and STOP** (.6/.8) — `sys_exit_group`
#   (`sys_exit` is exit(2) and ends only the calling thread, so the
#   idiomatic epilogue HUNG any threaded program: measured 124 vs 42);
#   `async_await_readable_ms(fd, ms)` so a cooperative accept loop can
#   observe a shutdown flag, returning 1 readable / 0 timeout instead
#   of the old constant 0; `thread_create_detached` + `thread_is_done`
#   (100 unjoined threads leaked 210,124,800 B of VA, now 0); and the
#   `thread_join` lost-wakeup deadlock — it read the tid word TWICE per
#   iteration under a comment claiming they were "in lockstep", ~1 join
#   in 150k, permanent and silent.
# - **Portable filesystem + process wrappers** (.7) — `sys_chdir`,
#   `signal_default`, and the `x*` family `xmkdir` / `xmkdir_p` /
#   `xsymlink` / `xreadlink` / `xlink`. Plus the ≥1000 PRIVATE ALIAS
#   band on aarch64, for source numbers no OS mints (`SYS_CHDIR = 1049`,
#   `SYS_FCHOWNAT = 1054` = 1000 + the native number, so the alias
#   documents itself) — needed because the native numbers were already
#   consumed by load-bearing x86-compat shims.
#   ⭐ SEVEN of these were found ONLY by a test that RUNS on the hosts
#   (`tests/tcyr/vr01_syscall_wrappers.tcyr`), and FIVE were HALF-FIXES
#   that stopped at the first symptom: `AT_FDCWD` fixed without its
#   sibling `AT_*` flag VALUES, `STAT_SIZE` without the rest of the
#   Darwin-188 layout, `unlink` without `rmdir`, three of four link
#   syscalls mapped. `xrmdir` had never worked on macOS-arm64 since the
#   day it shipped. A compile-only gate proves most of the risk and
#   catches almost none of the bugs.
# - **`#@incdir` entry-file-relative includes** (.7) — a source in a
#   subfolder can finally include its neighbour. CWD-first, so nothing
#   that resolves today changes meaning; the marker is in-band, read
#   only at byte 0, and must be relative + `..`-free (an absolute one
#   would rebuild the read-anything primitive CVE-16 removed).
# - **`alloc_reset` no longer invalidates the allocator** (.7) —
#   `default_alloc()` cached its vtable INSIDE the bump arena that
#   reset is for, so every subsequent call returned a dangling pointer.
# - **Arenas can be exhausted safely** (.9) — the growable arena and
#   the `ARENA_FULL_NULL|GROW|SPILL|ABORT` policy, which are ONE field,
#   not three features. `NULL` remains the default so no existing arena
#   moves. The bug was never the 0 return; it was that a `Str` of 0 is
#   indistinguishable from a valid one, so exhaustion surfaced as a
#   SIGSEGV several layers away.
# - **The uncontended mutex stopped entering the kernel** (.9) — a
#   three-state futex cell (0 free / 1 held / 2 held-with-waiters):
#   392 → 48 ns, on the primitive every lock-guarded structure in the
#   stdlib sits on. The roadmap had this blocked on `atomic_swap` +
#   a value-returning CAS; that premise was wrong — a SUCCESSFUL
#   boolean `atomic_cas(m, 1, 0)` already proves the pre-value was 1.
# - **`alloc_via` stopped being two-thirds call plumbing** (.10) —
#   15.1 → 11 ns by reading the vtable inline and dropping three
#   pass-through frames (cyrius does not inline, so each was real).
# - **`i64::MIN` formatted as a bare `-`** (.8) — 12 sites, not the 7
#   the roadmap named, including two inside the compiler. `n = 0 - n`
#   is a no-op at `i64::MIN`, so every decimal formatter emitted the
#   sign byte and nothing else and bayan serialised `{"n":-}`.
# - **Tooling honesty pass** (.7/.8/.10) — `cyrius test`/`bench`/`fuzz`
#   honour a subfolder callout and walk recursively; `coverage` grew
#   its corpus instead of silently truncating and finally counts
#   `pub fn`; `doc`/`vet`/`deny`/`audit`/`coverage` stopped absorbing
#   a bogus argument and exiting 0; `distlib --all` / `--check`; and
#   the `.deps` sidecar now unions the DECLARED `[deps] stdlib` with
#   the include-scan, because under-reporting it silently DISABLED
#   `cyrius deps`' consumer check.
#
# ─── v6.4.x CLOSEOUT (v6.4.82, 2026-07-27) ───
# The minor closes on a correctness burst, not a feature burst. What a
# USER of the language gets that they did not have at v6.4.0:
# - **Scalar float completion** (.55/.56/.57): `f64` as a fn RETURN type
#   (xmm0, sentinel -9); f32 scalar `+ - * /` and REAL comparisons on
#   x86/PE/Mach-O/aarch64-NEON/cx; float params + compound assign; a
#   WARN-only float typecheck that catches `x + 1` meaning "add the
#   denormal whose bits are 1". `f32` is still NOT a legal return type.
# - **Diagnostics** (.60/.62/.78): `line:COLUMN` + source excerpt +
#   caret on every error and warning; MANY errors per compile via
#   panic-mode recovery; NO output file when any error fired; a
#   `PEEKT` watchdog + EOF clamp so hostile or truncated input can
#   never hang the compiler (166,670 error lines → 5).
# - **Reserved words are a 67-name CLASS** (.77): `TOKNAME_BUILTIN` is
#   the single source of truth and `IS_KEYWORD_TOK` derives from it, so
#   the parser NAMES the intrinsic you collided with. 67 tokens used to
#   report `got unknown`; a consumer lost a 312-assertion suite to it.
# - **Caps** (.75/.76): identifier pool 256 KB → **512 KB** (524288 B,
#   LEX threshold 524016); the fn_table capacity warning now measures
#   against the fixed **32768** ceiling instead of the DOUBLING live cap
#   (it used to go silent exactly when corruption started). 8192 is
#   still the correct fn_table INITIAL cap — a blanket 8192→32768 sweep
#   would introduce errors.
# - **Const-expression correctness** (.74/.80/.81): four separate
#   occurrences of one `_cfo` const-fold-rewind mechanism, each found
#   after the previous was called complete — `100 >>> 1 + 1` == 2,
#   `1 - 2 + 3` == 5 (10 % of 3-term const exprs), and struct
#   operator-overload `p * 3 + 1` == 4. If you pinned a workaround
#   around any of these, drop it.
# - **Security** (.81): CVE-32/33/34 — three unbounded copies reachable
#   from untrusted source (an `include` of a 31490-char path SIGSEGV'd
#   cycc) — plus CVE-35/36 (fixed `/tmp` literals in the CLI).
# - **Tooling**: `cyrius coverage` now reports on the PROJECT's own
#   `src/` rather than the vendored stdlib (.72, `--full` restores the
#   old behaviour, `--min` gates CI); `cyrius audit` no longer fmt/lint
#   walks a consumer's vendored `lib/` (.78); `thread_local_alloc()`
#   ends hardcoded thread-local slot collisions (.65); crash-safe
#   `file_write_atomic` / `file_rename` / `xfsync` /
#   `file_create_exclusive` (.57); `lib/chrono.cyr` DateTime/Duration/
#   strftime (.67).
# - **Heap-region count**: 100 through .74 → 94 at .75 (six fn-indexed
#   side tables went lazy-alloc) → 100 again at .81, but by a DIFFERENT
#   route: the auditor's size parser was fixed to see unit-suffixed
#   entries it had been silently skipping. Do not read the matching
#   number as "the old 100 was right all along".
#
# ─── v6.4.0 (OPENS v6.4.x, 2026-07-03) ───
# HEADLINE: the CYRIUS_MONOMORPH default-on flip — generics (fns +
# structs, scalar + struct type-args, explicit + inferred receivers,
# cross-target x86/aarch64) now compile with NO env flag;
# CYRIUS_MONOMORPH=0 is the opt-out. Byte-identical: cycc has zero
# generic fns, so flag-on cycc == flag-off cycc (1,024,552 B UNCHANGED).
# The flip needed two prerequisites — decouple monomorph from _INLINE_OK
# (gate inline-capture to GFTP(S,fi)!=0, else +25.6% x86 size) and narrow
# the v6.3.29 frame-trim to GFTP!=0. async/await stays gated
# (CYRIUS_ASYNC=1); only monomorph flipped. Also folded sakshi 2.4.2 →
# 2.4.4 (128-bit W3C trace-id: sakshi_trace_set_128 / _id_hi / _id_lo).
# check.sh 128, self_compile 559 ms.
#
# ─── v6.3.x cycle (CLOSED at v6.3.45; v6.4.0 opened the v6.4.x minor) ───
# The "language trio" minor: non-capturing closures (.7) + lexical
# capture by value (.8); generic FUNCTIONS + STRUCTS via
# monomorphization (.9/.10 introduced gated, finalized .39; the
# CYRIUS_MONOMORPH default-on flip SHIPPED at v6.4.0 — generics are
# now DEFAULT-ON, CYRIUS_MONOMORPH=0 opts out); async/await as first-class Futures (.11,
# gated CYRIUS_ASYNC=1). Plus W^X userland ELF (.12), the
# initialized-globals cap 1024 → 4096 (.41), #derive(Serialize) f64
# fields (.40), and a long default-path correctness sweep (.33–.39:
# sub-i64 signed loads, >8 B struct-by-value params, &&/|| precedence
# split, the generics-engine repairs). Closeout state: cycc
# 1,024,552 B, self_compile ~565 ms, check.sh 128 gates, DCE floor
# 61 unreachable fns / 24,239 B, heap map 135 region entries /
# 56 live regions / 0 overlaps. Cross-OS self-host on REAL hardware
# (ecb macOS / cass Windows / pi aarch64) is a STANDING release gate
# — a green CI check is not it (v6.3.43/.44 both caught silent rot
# — Windows file-I/O and aarch64-macOS getpid — only by running on
# the hardware). See features.cyml (closures / generics / async /
# derive) + field_notes/compiler/gotchas.cyml.
#
# v6.1.x ("Backend Codegen Multi-Arc") shipped through .41: PIE
# position-independent codegen on x86_64 (.6) + aarch64 (.8) via
# --pie/CYRIUS_PIE=1; the .gnu.hash dynamic-link migration (.9);
# Phase D — the TS/TSX → JS emitter `cycc --emit-js` (.11, on the
# AST allocator fix .10) + `cyrius build --target=js` (.12); the
# Windows-pillar pack (.16-.18): PE var-syscall runtime dispatch +
# `lib/sync.cyr` portable mutex (.16), `nanosleep(35)`→Sleep (.17),
# and the Windows directory-listing port — `dir_list`/`is_dir`/
# `dir_walk` via FindFirstFileW + `lib/fs_win.cyr` (.18); the
# bayan + ganita data/math stdlib carve (.25/.26); the binary
# output cap raise 2 MB → 16 MB (.27); native TLS (over sigil)
# promoted to the DEFAULT transport — libssl now opt-OUT (.21);
# the lib/sys.cyr system-introspection carve (.28); Ed25519
# server certs for native TLS via the sigil 3.7.x fold (.31);
# the const chained-multiply fold fix (.37); and the Phase-F
# security-hardening arc — the dep-resolver / include-injection
# class (CVE-14/15/16, .33), the live-silent-failure cluster
# (CVE-22/23/31, .34/.35), the distlib un-inlined-include strip
# (.36), TLS-authn hardening (CVE-17/18/19/30, .36), and the
# local-symbol-table pack. See retros/v61x.cyml.
# api-surface continues to grow with per-cycle additions —
# v5.11.x added the per-repo isolation surface (cyrius.cyml
# [package].cyrius field + version-resolved CLI dispatch), the
# parser-to-emit named-op refactor with drift-gate, ELF64
# kernel emit + multiboot2 + EFI64-entry tag, the UEFI
# Application PE emit arc (gnoboot MVP unblocker), the
# byte-array literal syntax (.51), `fn efi_main(handle, st)`
# entry convention (.52), the cycc-side cyml pin-drift check
# (.57), the wrapper `lib sync` / `--strict-pin` / `--version`
# manifest-pin enhancements (.58), the DCE-aware undef-fn
# reachability filter cross-arch (.59), agnos gvar-init-order
# static-init tables (.64), the two-binary rename ceremony at
# v6.0.0 (cyrc → cybs + cc5 → cycc; back-compat symlinks for
# the v6.0.x window), CVE-05 tok_names mangle-path guard
# (.65), bridge-compiler retirement (.66; chain shortened to
# seed → cyrc → cc5), build-cc5-verify.sh fixpoint verifier
# script (.67), and the heap-map full reorganization (.68; brk
# 86.6 → 77.6 MB). See retros/v511x.cyml for the cycle
# narrative including the v5.x_cycle_close summary.
#
# v5.11.x highlights (in-flight, 59 slots through 2026-05-17):
# - IRON-BOOT PAPERCUT 4-SLOT ARC (.56-.59): filing
#   2026-05-16 with 4 items (LSP false-positive flood,
#   undef-fn "will crash" wording, wrapper/manifest pin drift,
#   shadow-lib note over-fires). Closed cleanly across the
#   absorber band per user split-by-surface direction. .56:
#   LSP forks `cyrius check --with-deps` wrapper (was: raw
#   cycc, NULL envp, no [deps.*] resolution); undef-fn
#   `(will crash at runtime)` → `(call site may be
#   unreachable)` cross-arch. .57: cycc `_check_cyml_pin_drift`
#   surfaces toolchain drift via env-tunable
#   `CYRIUS_NO_WARN_PIN_DRIFT` / `CYRIUS_STRICT_PIN`;
#   shadow-lib note rewritten as content-compare (was:
#   directory-existence). .58: wrapper polish (`cyrius lib
#   sync`, `--strict-pin` flag, `--version` manifest-pin line)
#   + `scripts/version-bump.sh` rebuild fix for the wrapper
#   that had been stuck embedding .25 since 2026-05-12. .59:
#   DCE-aware reachability filter cross-arch — aarch64 gained
#   full DCE bitmap pass (mirrors x86 since v5.10.x) so
#   `vec_get`-from-dead-`vec_find` style refs stay silent.
# - BYTE-ARRAY LITERAL + EFI_MAIN CONVENTION (.51-.53):
#   `var foo[N] = { 0x.., ... };` literal feeds gnoboot's EFI
#   GUIDs + UTF-16LE strings. `fn efi_main(handle, st)`
#   convention auto-trampolines firmware args. v5.11.53
#   hotfix for MR-form `mov r/m64, r64` REX prefix typo
#   (`0x4C → 0x49`) — gotcha worth remembering: MR-form puts
#   dst in r/m field, src in reg field; REX.B (not REX.R)
#   extends the dst.
# - UEFI APPLICATION PE EMIT ARC (.47-.49): 3-slot arc
#   unblocking the AGNOS sovereign UEFI bootloader gnoboot
#   (~2000 LoC of cyrius replacing GRUB on the boot path).
#   `_TARGET_EFI_APPLICATION` flag + `CYRIUS_TARGET_EFI=1`
#   env var. Subsystem 3 → 10 (EFI_APPLICATION). EEXIT emits
#   single 0xC3 (ret) under EFI mode — firmware reads rax as
#   EFI_STATUS. ExitProcess import skipped; Data Dirs [1]/[12]
#   zeroed; NX_COMPAT forced; RELOCS_STRIPPED cleared (latter
#   was the v5.11.49 OVMF runtime smoke discovery — UEFI
#   firmware treats the bit as exact-ImageBase-or-fail).
#   `_pe_register_kernel32` 9-fn refactor squeeze-in at .47.
#   New `programs/efi_probe.cyr` (.48) boots end-to-end under
#   qemu+OVMF (.49 runtime smoke gate green).
# - ELF64 KERNEL EMIT + AGREEMENT FIX (.43-.46): EMITELF64_KERNEL
#   for AGNOS UEFI x86_64 boot (Path A). v5.11.46 fixed FIXUP↔
#   EMITELF64_KERNEL entry-arithmetic mismatch (`kmode==1`
#   branch hardcoded 0x100060 ELF32+mb1 layout vs the new ELF64+
#   mb2 0x1000A8). Path A subsequently dead-on-iron due to GRUB
#   `grub_relocator64_efi_boot` W^X bug under modern UEFI;
#   replaced by Path C (gnoboot, .47-.49).
# - PARSER-TO-EMIT NAMED-OP REFACTOR + DRIFT GATE (.35-.39):
#   per-backend EMIT_<OP> helpers replace direct `EB(S, 0xXX)`
#   byte emits in `parse_*.cyr`. Classes B (PIC-vs-direct
#   address loads), C (f64 unary ops), D (v5.7.12 audit doc).
#   v5.11.39 drift gate scans for any remaining EB(S,...) and
#   fails check.sh. Structurally locks the refactor.
# - ELF SECTION-HEADER PARITY SWEEP (.29-.34): kernel + user-bin
#   ELF emitters across all 5 instantiations (x86 user/kernel,
#   aarch64 user/kernel, cyrld linker) brought to section-header
#   parity for GRUB compatibility + tooling acceptance.
# - PER-REPO ISOLATION ARC (.17 + .25 + .26): three-part close
#   on the snapshot-ping-pong wipe vector. (.17) `cbt/deps.cyr`
#   stdlib_dir resolution rewritten: dev-mode-first (./lib when
#   src/main.cyr exists) → cyrius.cyml-pinned snapshot → legacy
#   global fallback. (.25) `cyrius` CLI now reads cyrius.cyml
#   `[package].cyrius` field and re-execs to the matching
#   `~/.cyrius/versions/<pin>/bin/cyrius` with CYRIUS_RESOLVED=1
#   loop guard. (.26) `cyriusly use 5.11.X` defaults to writing
#   cyrius.cyml's pin instead of `~/.cyrius/current`; `--global`
#   keeps the legacy global-pointer write. Sibling agents
#   flipping global state no longer affect other repos.
# - STDLIB ANNOTATION ARC (.1-.7): seven phases of return-type
#   annotations across native lib/ + per-arch syscall peers +
#   compiler internals.
# - 9-SIBLING FOLDIN CASCADE (.5): single-slot fold of vani /
#   patra / agnosys / sandhi / sakshi / sigil / yukti / sankoch /
#   niyama via the sandhi pattern; retired .cyrius-toolchain in
#   favor of cyrius.cyml [package].cyrius as the single version-
#   pin source of truth.
# - P(-1) HARDENING SWEEP (.45): 4-item bundle including
#   `_cc5_contamination_gate` (greps build/cc5 for mabda/wgpu
#   strings — the v5.11.43-style slip signature), `cyrius vet`
#   restored as real audit tool, dead-fn report gated behind
#   `CYRIUS_DCE_VERBOSE=1`, state.md compression 1451→583 lines.
# - LSP SEMANTIC TOKENS LOCALS+PARAMS (.42): textDocument/
#   semanticTokens/full now colors locals + parameters distinctly
#   from globals/fn-names/types. cyrius-lsp argv[0] self-resolution
#   (.44) via /proc/self/exe lets editors with minimal-env LSP
#   launchers find cycc without $CYRIUS_HOME / $HOME.
# - CVE-08 HARDENING + f64_abs PEEPHOLE (.40-.41): cld (0xFC)
#   emitted before any rep movsb/stosb to clear direction flag;
#   f64_abs(x) peephole replaces 6-instr sequence with 2-instr
#   ANDPS + RET.
#
# Additional v5.11.x highlights (front + middle, .1-.34):
# - STDLIB ANNOTATION ARC (.1-.7): seven phases of return-type
#   annotations across native lib/ + per-arch syscall peers +
#   compiler internals.
# - 9-SIBLING FOLDIN CASCADE (.5): single-slot fold of vani /
#   patra / agnosys / sandhi / sakshi / sigil / yukti / sankoch /
#   niyama via the sandhi pattern; retired .cyrius-toolchain in
#   favor of cyrius.cyml [package].cyrius as the single version-
#   pin source of truth.
# - PER-REPO ISOLATION ARC (.17 + .25 + .26): three-part close
#   on the snapshot-ping-pong wipe vector via cyrius.cyml
#   [package].cyrius + version-resolved CLI dispatch +
#   `cyriusly use --global` opt-in for legacy global writes.
# - PE/WIN64 PATH-API SURFACE (.21-.23): syscall 83/87/89 auto-
#   import + CreateDirectoryW/DeleteFileW dispatch (.21); UTF-16
