# ─── Core Reference (core.cyml) ─── 7 entries ──────────────────────
# What Cyrius is + how to use the toolchain.

# overview                — Sovereign self-hosting systems language; cycc binary; capabilities
# syntax                  — Variables, functions, control flow, operators, structs, slices, strings
# compiler_architecture   — Module layout, compilation flow, codegen model, optimization pipeline
# development_loop        — Proven workflow for adding features (research → vidya → build → test → audit → docs)
# known_limitations       — Active gotchas and grow-the-cap rules
# porting_guide           — How to add a new architecture backend (aarch64 example)
# stdlib                  — Module catalog with key APIs and dep bundles

# ─── Language Features (features.cyml) ─── 66 entries ──────────────
# How to use specific Cyrius language features. (The list below names the
# type/syntax entries; features.cyml also carries the per-release feature
# entries the index does not enumerate.)

# multi_width_types       — i8/i16/i32/i64/u128 with width-correct codegen
# sizeof_operator         — Compile-time size constants
# unions                  — Shared-offset variant fields
# bitfield_builtins       — bit_get/set/clear/toggle, popcount, ctz, clz
# struct_field_widths     — Per-field type annotations and offset rules
# expression_type_propagation — Mixing widths and pointer arithmetic
# defer_statement         — LIFO cleanup at function return (per-flag exit-path safe)
# ifplat_directive        — Sugar for #ifdef CYRIUS_ARCH_<UPPER>
# enum_namespacing        — Enum.VARIANT in any expression context
# ref_directive           — Compile-time TOML loading via #ref
# ret2_rethi              — Return two values via rax:rdx + native multi-return
# continue_in_for_loops   — continue with forward-patch
# derive_str_fields       — #derive(Serialize) + #derive(accessors)
# secret_var_compound_ops — Struct init, &local arch dispatch, #regalloc, secret var, attributes
# slice_type_v58x         — slice<T> / [T] first-class type with bounds-aware indexing
# relaxed_fn_ordering     — fn definitions can appear after top-level statements
# tagged_unions_v58x      — sum-type syntax: enum Result<T,E> { Ok(T), Err(E) } with multi-arg + nullary tagged variants
# exhaustive_match_v58x   — match-coverage check + arm-tag dedup (warning, not error; opt out via _ =>)
# type_system_real_phase_arc — Real type system (v5.10.x 5-phase): annotations, call-site checks, overload dispatch, sum-type rewriting
# typed_simd_value_type_abi  — f64v2 / f64v4 primitive value types: XMM/V register-pair param + return ABI per backend; PE pointer-form-only
# f32v4_packed_single_simd   — f32v4 128-bit packed single (4× f32): structured-descriptor SLTYPE (-2121, band ≤ -2048, _vec_desc), addps/subps/mulps, reuses f64v2 XMM ABI; complete on all four backends (Phase 1, v6.4.4 x86 SSE; aarch64 NEON v6.4.28; Win64 PE value-form v6.4.31; cx per-lane v6.4.32)
# integer_vector_simd        — i8v16/i16v8/i32v4/i64v2 (+ unsigned u*) 128-bit integer vectors: descriptor sentinels (signed = desc bit 1), iv_add/iv_sub/iv_mul(dst,a,b,n,w) width-literal → paddb/w/d/q; value-form typed ops (i32v4_add(a,b), param-mask class 1 = any 16-byte vector); iv_dp8 u8·i8→i32 widening dot (b1.58 GEMM); complete on all four backends (Phase 3a/3b, v6.4.6/v6.4.7 x86 SSE2; aarch64 NEON v6.4.30 EMIT_IVEC_BINOP/DP8; cx per-lane v6.4.32)
# f32v8_avx2_256bit_simd     — f32v8 256-bit SIMD (8× f32, one YMM): sentinel -2153, EMIT_F32V8_LOOP = f32v4 loop + 2-byte VEX prefix (vaddps/vsubps/vmulps ymm, tokens 147-149, first VEX/AVX in the toolchain); 256-bit value-return ABI generalized to _is_simd256 (byte-id f64v4); simd_has_avx2() CPUID probe + 2×SSE runtime fallback; x86 arith first landed at Phase 4 R1, v6.4.8. Phase 4 R2 (v6.4.9): f32v8_fma (vfmadd231ps ymm = C4 E2 7D B8 D1 — FMA3, the toolchain's FIRST 3-byte VEX; token 150) + f32v8_dot (token 151: 8-lane reduce via vextractf128 + L=0 vaddps fold, two-haddps can't cross the 128-bit split); simd_has_fma() = leaf-1 ECX bit 12 CPUID probe (a DIFFERENT bit than AVX2's leaf-7 EBX bit 5); PHASE 5 COMPLETE — f32v8 arith now runs on all four backends (aarch64 v6.4.29 via 2×128-bit NEON fallback = EMIT_F32V_LOOP, the aarch64 256-bit emitters staying return-0 stubs never reached at runtime; cx per-lane v6.4.32; simd_f32v8 XFAIL removed at v6.4.29). Native 256-bit stays x86-AVX2-only
# overload_dispatch_pointer_vs_value — `f64v2_add(&x, &y)` auto-routes to f64v2_add_ptr; value-form base for `f64v2_add(x, y)` (v5.10.39)
# f64_named_type_and_operators — `var x: f64` / `var x: f32` give bare `+ - * /` + REAL float comparisons (f64 v6.2.19, f32 ARITHMETIC v6.4.56 on x86/PE/Mach-O/aarch64-NEON/cx); scalar `f64` is a legal fn RETURN type (xmm0, sentinel -9, v6.4.55) but `f32` is NOT; float params + compound assign + a WARN-only typecheck (v6.4.57). Construct an f32 with `f32_from(f64_from(int))`, extract with `f64_to(f32_to(x))`
# reserved_word_class_toknames — reserved words are a CLASS of 67 builtin/intrinsic names (TOKNAME_BUILTIN in src/common/util.cyr) + the ~25 statement keywords; IS_KEYWORD_TOK DERIVES from the name table so the two sets can't drift; since v6.4.77 the parser NAMES the collision instead of "got unknown" (toks 79 and 111 are double-assigned and print both spellings)
# diagnostics_column_caret_multierror — `line:COLUMN` + source excerpt + caret on every error/warning (v6.4.60, packed into tok_lines' high 32 bits, zero new heap); MANY errors per compile via panic-mode recovery (v6.4.62); no output file if any error fired; PEEKT watchdog + EOF clamp so hostile/truncated input never hangs (v6.4.62/.78)
# cap_raises_v51118_v51119 — compiler capacity caps + history. CURRENT: identifier pool 524288 B (512 KB, v6.4.76, LEX guard 524016), fn_table init 8192 growable to a 32768 hard ceiling with the warning measured against the CEILING (v6.4.75), var_table 8192, fixup_table 1048576, code buffer 64 MiB growable
# visibility_public_private_v650 — file-scoped `private` + per-item `public`/`pub` (v6.5.0): opt-in per FILE, hard errors (not warnings) through the multi-error path, enforced on calls / tail calls / operator-overload dispatch / global-var reads, and private items drop out of the exported symbol table (lib/regex.cyr: 24 -> 14 exported symbols)
# arena_lifecycle_v51114 — arena_new/alloc/reset/free (v5.11.14) PLUS the v6.5.9 growable arena + ARENA_FULL_NULL|GROW|SPILL|ABORT exhaustion policy (one field, not three features; NULL stays the default so no existing arena moves; GROW retains its chunks across arena_reset by design)
# threads_detached_and_is_done_v658 — thread_create_detached / thread_is_done (v6.5.8), the thread_join lost-wakeup deadlock, and why sys_exit_group (v6.5.6) is the correct epilogue once any thread exists

# ─── Stdlib Modules (stdlib_modules.cyml) ─── 20 entries ───────────
# Per-module usage (APIs, gotchas, idioms). (The list below names the
# long-standing entries; the file also carries per-release module
# entries the index does not enumerate.)

# atoi_stdlib                   — Decimal string → integer
# f64_atan_and_math_lib         — f64_atan builtin and lib/math.cyr transcendentals
# base64_module                 — RFC 4648 encode/decode
# chrono_module                 — Clocks, sleep, ISO-8601 + the v6.4.67 DateTime handle / Duration API / strftime dt_format + dt_strptime (UTC only, bare epoch-ns i64)
# file_locking                  — lib/io.cyr: flock(2) wrappers + the v6.4.57 crash-safe write set (file_write_atomic / file_rename / xfsync / file_create_exclusive) + the portable x* family (xopen/xstat/xunlink/xgetdents/xlseek/xflock; xrmdir v6.5.2; xmkdir/xmkdir_p/xsymlink/xreadlink/xlink v6.5.7) and the Darwin AT_*-value + routing traps found by running them on real hardware
# thread_local_slot_allocator   — thread_local_alloc() (v6.4.65): allocate a per-thread slot, never hardcode an index; slots 0-15 frozen for legacy, allocated slots start at 16
# csv_module                    — RFC 4180 parse/write
# http_module                   — HTTP/1.0 client
# patra_stdlib_module           — Sovereign SQL database in stdlib
# strstr_function               — strstr / strchr / memchr
# hashmap_str_keys              — map_new_str() for Str-struct keys
# fncall_ceiling                — fncall0..fncall8 ABI rules and C-shim decision table
# identity_lookups_musl_pattern — pwd/grp/shadow/pam (NSS-free)

