# ─── Language Field Notes (field_notes/language/) ─── 43 entries ───
# User-facing gotchas that bite at parse time, at runtime, at the
# platform/ABI boundary, or in the stdlib. Refreshed at v6.4.82.

# parser_syntax.cyml       — 12 entries. `>>` is LOGICAL / `>>>` arithmetic;
#     bitwise_ops_share_the_additive_tier (VERIFIED tier table — `&`,`|`,`^`
#     on the +/- tier, `1 | 2 + 1` == 4, comparisons LOOSER than bitwise);
#     float_bit_intrinsics_cannot_flank_term_operators (`a * f64_from(2)` is
#     a parse ERROR — parenthesize or bind to a var); caret/minus (explanation
#     corrected, unary `~` DOES exist); var-redecl + comparisons-in-args (both
#     long since FIXED); var-bracket-must-be-literal; struct/enum bodies.
# semantics_runtime.cyml   — 11 entries. var_name_bracket_is_bytes_not_elements
#     (fn-local = N BYTES, TOP LEVEL = N i64 SLOTS — the CVE-34 shape; use
#     `var a: i64[N]`); string_literal_to_str_coercion_is_annotation_only (a
#     bare literal into an UNTYPED param is a raw cstr and every str_* call on
#     it silently returns nothing — annotate `: Str`); fn main is not the entry
#     point; global init order; bump-allocator lifetime.
# diagnostics_caps.cyml    — 6 entries. live_compiler_capacity_ceilings (the
#     numbers that are actually live: identifier pool 524288 B, fn_table
#     8192→32768, and why a blanket 8192→32768 sweep is WRONG);
#     diagnostics_carry_column_excerpt_and_dont_stop_at_the_first_error;
#     the gvar wall; the output-buffer ceiling; --strict.
# platform_abi.cyml        — 6 entries. Per-OS target flags; struct-by-value
#     return; varargs; the fncall6-into-extern-C ceiling (PREMISE-CHECK
#     banner — predates the v6.4.64 Win64 stack-arg fix, and pure cyrius has
#     NO arity limit); aarch64 clobber + immediate limits; the agnos mirror.
# stdlib_format.cyml       — 5 entries. str_data is NOT NUL-terminated (+ the
#     `: Str` coercion rule); toml quote stripping; cstr-key migration; CYML
#     format; the sandhi service-layer dep.
# shell_runtime.cyml       — 3 entries. Bash gotchas hit during content work.
